{"archetypes":[{"name":"kv-stdout-format","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan's parsers assume exact KEY=VALUE line formats from rebase-push.sh and check-phantom-dirty.sh; any mismatch silently misparsing real output would corrupt REBASE_OUTCOME/PHANTOM_STATUS routing with no error signal.","prompt_body":"Read `scripts/rebase-push.sh` and `scripts/check-phantom-dirty.sh` to verify that the exact KV key names and stdout format the plan's wrapper parser assumes — `SKIPPED_ALREADY_PUSHED=true`, `SKIPPED_ALREADY_FRESH=true`, `CONFLICT_FILES=<comma-list>`, `STATUS=<value>`, `PHANTOM_COUNT=<n>`, `PHANTOM_PATHS_FILE=<path>`, `REASON=<value>` — are actually emitted by those scripts as bare `KEY=VALUE` lines on stdout. Check whether `rebase-push.sh` emits conflict-file information on stdout, via a different key name, or exclusively through exit code, and whether the plan's defensive `git diff --name-only --diff-filter=U` fallback triggers under realistic conditions or only in a narrow edge case the existing script never exercises. Confirm that `check-phantom-dirty.sh` emits the `STATUS=tracked-only` variant that `lib-phantom-probe.sh`'s branch table lists alongside `STATUS=clean`, since a missing branch arm would fall through to the `STATUS=phantom` path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"denylist-anchor-match","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"If the lint-foreground-markers.sh linter matches bare filenames but SKILL.md fences use ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/... invocation form, the new DENYLIST entries will silently never fire, voiding the CI safety net the plan relies on.","prompt_body":"Read `scripts/lint-foreground-markers.sh` to determine the exact anchor-detection pattern the linter uses — specifically whether it matches on the bare filename (e.g., `rebase-checkpoint-probe.sh`) or requires a full path prefix, and whether shell variable expansions like `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` in a fence line are handled or cause the match to miss. Verify that the DENYLIST heredoc at the line range the plan cites (currently L18-28) accepts entries exactly as written (`rebase-checkpoint-probe.sh` and `phantom-probe-with-warn.sh` as bare names) and that the insertion point and ordering convention the plan describes match the file's actual format. Cross-check against the per-anchor comment rule: for a fence whose anchor line contains `"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/rebase-checkpoint-probe.sh"`, confirm the linter's five-line look-back window will find a `# Foreground required: see BASH_AUTHORING.md §4` comment placed as the plan directs before the rehydration boilerplate. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-pivot-gap","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan pivots test-implement-rebase-macro.sh invariants C/G/H and adds J, but does not verify existing assertion patterns use content-matching rather than line-number anchors that will break when Region 1 and Region 2 deletions shift SKILL.md's line offsets.","prompt_body":"Read `scripts/test-implement-rebase-macro.sh` to identify the exact assertion forms for invariants C, G, H, and I — specifically whether any grep patterns reference SKILL.md by line number (which the plan's ~55-net-line deletion will invalidate) versus by content string. Verify that the revised invariant H — asserting `--no-push --skip-if-pushed --keep-on-conflict` appears exactly once in `scripts/rebase-checkpoint-probe.sh` and zero times in SKILL.md — does not accidentally match the bare `--no-push` invocations the plan says remain in SKILL.md for `step8b_rebase`, given that `grep` for `--skip-if-pushed` would not catch those, but a looser `--no-push` pattern would over-count. Confirm that the new invariant J (assert exactly 2 `phantom-probe-with-warn.sh --step` invocation lines in SKILL.md) can be expressed using the harness's existing assertion style, and check whether the harness has a helper or inline grep pattern that handles the `"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/..."` quoting form reliably. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
